ICVSP — Platform Alternatives Research

# 1. Strong Supabase alternatives — capability comparison

# 2. What matters most for ICVSP?

• Best direct substitutes: Nhost and Appwrite Native PostgreSQL. Both retain SQL + PostGIS + realtime/auth; migration still means rebuilding schema, API integration and access policies.

• Firebase is not the best fit for the core hazard database: realtime is strong, but the NoSQL model and geohash workaround make relational evidence/reputation/history and spatial filtering less straightforward.

• Historical analytics: PostgreSQL is the practical fit. Keep timestamped beacons/reports/evidence as append-only history, index event_time + device_id/hazard_id, and add time partitions/aggregations when volume justifies it. A separate warehouse/time-series service is not needed for the MVP.

• Geospatial is a key differentiator: use PostGIS for distance, bounding boxes, nearby hazards and map-matching filters. It supports indexed spatial queries; simple latitude/longitude columns alone will become limiting.

4. Existing Supabase limits — when could they become a problem?

# 5. Email limit: keep Supabase Auth, add an SMTP provider

Supabase built-in SMTP is test-only: 2 emails/hour per project and sends only to team-authorized addresses. Custom SMTP removes the built-in provider restriction; Supabase initially applies a 30 emails/hour Auth limit, adjustable in Authentication > Rate Limits. The email provider’s own quota still applies. Supabase Auth continues to handle signup, verification and password reset.

# 6. Recommendation — what should ICVDP use?

Keep the current stack for the MVP: Supabase PostgreSQL + Auth + Realtime, with FastAPI hosted on AWS Lightsail (start at $7/mo) and Resend Free for Auth emails. This avoids a costly migration and preserves the existing schema/team work.

• Lowest practical development cost: Supabase Free + AWS Lightsail $7/mo + Resend Free = about $7/mo (but Supabase may pause; no automatic backups).

• More production-ready baseline: Supabase Pro $25 + Lightsail $7 + Resend Free = about $32/mo, before taxes, optional add-ons and usage overages.

• Revisit Nhost/Appwrite only if Supabase limits or pricing become a measured issue. Before migrating, benchmark real beacon rate, concurrent alert subscribers, database growth, egress and geospatial query latency.

• Security actions before production: enable RLS on every exposed table; write least-privilege policies for users/devices; keep service-role/API secrets only in FastAPI environment secrets; use TLS, backups, MFA for admins, and test unauthorized reads/writes.

